            <ArticleTitle>Vasospastic angina and scombroid syndrome: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>222-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Scombroid syndrome is a fish poisoning characterised by the onset of symptoms compatible with a pseudoallergic reaction; it is rarely also responsible of signs and symptoms of acute coronary syndromes, as demonstrated in this case report.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
